,"name":"Asbury Avenue / New Jersey Avenue"},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-74.009783,40.2143597]}},{"type":"Feature","properties":{"resourceCoords":[3019.6,3246.9],"name":"Asbury Avenue / Pennsylvania Avenue"},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-74.0088303,40.2146137]}},{"type":"Feature","properties":{"resourceCoords":[4068.9,4792.6],"name":"Asbury Avenue / New York Avenue"},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-74.0078827,40.2148671]}},{"type":"Feature","properties":{"resourceCoords":[6426.7,8249.1],"name":"Asbury Avenue / Pilgrim Pathway"},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-74.0057675,40.215439]}},{"type":"Feature","properties":{"resourceCoords":[380.0,1696.0],"name":"Mount Tabor Way / New Jersey Avenue"},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-74.0100128,40.2137278]}},{"type":"Feature","properties":{"resourceCoords":[1402.8,9691.2],"name":"Central Avenue / McClintock Street"},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-74.005733,40.2132771]}},{"type":"Feature","properties":{"resourceCoords":[1410.1,8180.7],"name":"McClintock Street / Pilgrim Pathway"},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-74.0065162,40.2134454]}},{"type":"Feature","properties":{"resourceCoords":[1435.3,3234.5],"name":"Mount Carmel Way / Pennsylvania Avenue"},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-74.0090627,40.2139853]}},{"type":"Feature","properties":{"resourceCoords":[1429.1,4763.9],"name":"Mount Carmel Way / New York Avenue"},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-74.0082659,40.2138158]}},{"type":"Feature","properties":{"resourceCoords":[1406.2,7186.8],"name":"Mount Carmel Way / Pilgrim Pathway"},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-74.0070068,40.2135467]}},{"type":"Feature","properties":{"resourceCoords":[352.8,7181.0],"name":"Mount Tabor Way / Pilgrim Pathway / Pitman Avenue"},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-74.0071558,40.2131198]}},{"type":"Feature","properties":{"resourceCoords":[370.2,4754.2],"name":"Mount Tabor Way / New York Avenue"},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-74.0084223,40.2133869]}},{"type":"Feature","properties":{"resourceCoords":[377.7,3223.4],"name":"Mount Tabor Way / Pennsylvania Avenue"},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-74.0092209,40.2135579]}},{"type":"Feature","properties":{"resourceCoords":[329.1,9677.8],"name":"Central Avenue / Pitman Avenue"},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-74.0058899,40.2128511]}},{"type":"Feature","properties":{"resourceCoords":[4724.2,8233.3],"name":"Bath Avenue / Pilgrim Pathway"},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-74.0060202,40.2147727]}},{"type":"Feature","properties":{"resourceCoords":[4710.1,9724.8],"name":"Bath Avenue / Central Avenue"},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-74.0052468,40.2146072]}},{"type":"Feature","properties":{"resourceCoords":[2502.5,3248.1],"name":"Mount Zion Way / Pennsylvania Avenue"},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-74.0089034,40.214416]}},{"type":"Feature","properties":{"resourceCoords":[2489.3,4773.7],"name":"Mount Zion Way / New York Avenue"},"geometry":{"type":"Point","coordinates":[-74.0081096,40.2142448]}}]}}},"metadata":{"sheet-47":{"description":"Sheet 47 covers the southern half of West Ocean Grove, the strip of Neptune Township between the New York and Long Branch Railroad and the western edge of the Ocean Grove camp meeting grounds. The railroad tracks run down the left margin. Beside them lies a small industrial district along a street lettered West Ocean Grove: the Standard Oil Co. depot, the Charles Lewis Lumber & Hardware yard with its lumber warehouse and sheds, Palmateer Bros. lumber and hardware yard, an ice house of the Independent Ice Co., the Excelsior Steam Laundry and the Asbury Park Pumping Station with its compressors, filter house, wells and a reservoir. Corlies Avenue and 12th Avenue reach the railroad here. East of South Main a curving drive with a central circle and the Middle Gate and South Gate lead into a grid of large surveyed but mostly empty blocks between Lawrence, Benson, Whitefield and Delaware avenues, crossed by Embury, Webb, Abbott, Broadway, Cookman, Clark, Franklin and Stockton avenues. Most lots south of Broadway are vacant; houses stand chiefly between Embury and Cookman avenues, and the Ocean Grove Green Houses occupy a lot on Webb Avenue. Fletcher Avenue and the shore of Fletcher Lake close the sheet at the bottom. Water pipes of 4 to 12 inches are drawn in the streets, with a 12 inch connecting main from the pumping station. The sheet is drawn at 60 feet to an inch, with north toward the upper right of the page.","notes":["S. Main is South Main Street today.","Delaware Avenue lies along the right edge, with only its west side drawn.","Broadway junctions were not detected; the street is drawn as a wide boulevard.","West Ocean Grove south: railroad, lumber yards, pumping station, South Main, Lawrence/Benson/Whitefield/Delaware Av from Embury to Fletcher Av. 60 ft scale, one part, north upper right (rotation about -15)."],"streetnames":["Embury Avenue","Webb Avenue","Abbott Avenue","Broadway","Cookman Avenue","Clark Avenue","Franklin Avenue","Stockton Avenue","Fletcher Avenue","Lawrence Avenue","Benson Avenue","Whitefield Avenue","Delaware Avenue","South Main","Corlies Avenue","12th Avenue"],"placenames":["West Ocean Grove","Ocean Grove","Fletcher Lake"]},"sheet-48":{"description":"Sheet 48 covers the northern half of West Ocean Grove, in Neptune Township, between the New York and Long Branch Railroad and Delaware Avenue, from Wesley Lake and Lake Avenue in the north to Abbott Avenue. On the left the railroad, Springwood Avenue and the borough line with Asbury Park cross the top corner; a commercial row along a street lettered West Ocean Grove faces the tracks, with coal yards of G. P. Farmer Coal & Supply Co. and Consumers Coal & Supply Co., the United Ice Co.'s ice factory (in operation during the summer season only), the J. B. Hurley wood working shop, stores, restaurants, a club room and a rescue mission. Main and South Main run north and south past Evergreen Park and the head of Wesley Lake. East of South Main stand the Neptune Township High School, the S. J. Rogers livery and the North Gate, and then a residential grid between Lawrence, Benson, Whitefield and Delaware avenues crossed by Mount Tabor Way, Mount Hermon Way, Main, Heck, Embury and Webb avenues. Embury Avenue is drawn offset at Benson Avenue: the western stretch lies about 90 feet north of the eastern one. A large association yard with wagon sheds fills part of the block east of Whitefield Avenue. Lake Avenue and Asbury Avenue run along the lake at the top right. Scale 60 feet to an inch.","notes":["Main is today's Main Street; S. Main is South Main Street.","Embury Avenue east of Benson Avenue is drawn about 90 ft south of its west part; the modern street is straight, so the Delaware Avenue junction was left out.","West Ocean Grove north: railroad, Main/South Main, Neptune Township High School, Lawrence to Delaware Av from Lake Av to Abbott Av. Embury Av drawn offset at Benson. 60 ft scale, one part."],"streetnames":["Lake Avenue","Springwood Avenue","Main","South Main","Lawrence Avenue","Benson Avenue","Whitefield Avenue","Delaware Avenue","Mount Tabor Way","Mount Hermon Way","Main Avenue","Heck Avenue","Embury Avenue","Webb Avenue","Abbott Avenue","Asbury Avenue"],"placenames":["West Ocean Grove","Ocean Grove","Wesley Lake","Evergreen Park","Asbury Park"]},"sheet-49":{"description":"Sheet 49 covers the south-western part of the Ocean Grove camp meeting grounds, from Delaware Avenue on the west to Central Avenue on the east and from Fletcher Lake to Abbott Avenue. Fletcher Lake runs along the left edge and bottom left, with Fletcher Avenue following its shore. The cross streets Fletcher, Inskip, Stockton, Franklin, Clark and Cookman avenues, Broadway and Abbott Avenue run between Delaware, New Jersey, Pennsylvania and New York avenues, Pilgrim Pathway and Central Avenue. The blocks are cut into narrow lots of summer cottages and boarding houses, many named on the map, among them the Bancroft Rest Home, Grays Hotel, Norene Cottage, the Chautauqua, the Holly, the Laurel, the Broadmoor, the Melrose, the Rosemont, the Lake View and the Ocean View House. A row of small cottages fills the block between Inskip and Stockton avenues, and an open square lettered Park Heights lies between Pennsylvania and New York avenues east of Clark Avenue. The western blocks near the lake are only partly built. Broadway is drawn as a wide street. Water pipes run in most streets. Scale 60 feet to an inch.","notes":["Fletcher Avenue along the lake is Fletcher Lake Avenue today.","Broadway junctions were not detected.","Ocean Grove south-west: Delaware to Central Av, Fletcher Lake to Abbott Av. 60 ft scale, one part (rotation about 74)."],"streetnames":["Delaware Avenue","New Jersey Avenue","Pennsylvania Avenue","New York Avenue","Pilgrim Pathway","Central Avenue","Fletcher Avenue","Inskip Avenue","Stockton Avenue","Franklin Avenue","Clark Avenue","Cookman Avenue","Broadway","Abbott Avenue"],"placenames":["Ocean Grove","Fletcher Lake","Park Heights"]},"sheet-50":{"description":"Sheet 50 is drawn upside down on the page (its sheet number is at the bottom left). It covers the centre of the Ocean Grove camp meeting grounds, between Central Avenue and Delaware Avenue and between Mount Tabor Way and Pitman Avenue on the north and Abbott Avenue on the south. North-south streets Delaware, New Jersey, Pennsylvania and New York avenues, Pilgrim Pathway and Central Avenue are crossed by Mount Tabor Way, Mount Hermon Way, Main, Heck, Embury, Webb and Abbott avenues, with Pitman Avenue and Olin Street east of Pilgrim Pathway. The block between Pitman Avenue, Olin Street and Central Avenue is the commercial heart of the grounds, with stores, an ice cream factory, the Ocean Grove Times printing office, a fire company house and the Ocean Grove Camp Meeting Association building with its bank and offices. Main Avenue carries boarding houses and hotels such as the National, the Centennial and the Somerset. St. Paul's M. E. Church stands between Embury and Webb avenues at New York Avenue. The remaining blocks are small summer cottages on narrow lots. Scale 60 feet to an inch.","notes":["The sheet is printed rotated 180 degrees on the page.","Pilgrim Pathway at Pitman Avenue has two modern nodes 44 m apart; the one the sheet does not draw was excluded.","Ocean Grove centre: Mt Tabor/Pitman to Abbott, Delaware to Central Av; printed upside down (rotation about -105). 60 ft scale, one part."],"streetnames":["Central Avenue","Pilgrim Pathway","New York Avenue","Pennsylvania Avenue","New Jersey Avenue","Delaware Avenue","Pitman Avenue","Olin Street","Mount Tabor Way","Mount Hermon Way","Main Avenue","Heck Avenue","Embury Avenue","Webb Avenue","Abbott Avenue"],"placenames":["Ocean Grove"]},"sheet-51":{"description":"Sheet 51 covers the ocean front of Ocean Grove from McClintock Street to Broadway, between Central Avenue and the beach. Cross streets Pitman Avenue, Olin, Main, Heck, Embury, Webb and Abbott avenues run from Central Avenue past Beach Avenue to Ocean Avenue, which is drawn with only its west side and the board walk beyond it. The blocks are filled with summer hotels and boarding houses, many named: the Sunset Lodge, Atlantic House, Hotel Grand, the Alaska (open all year), the Mulford, the Waterbury, the United States Hotel, Main Avenue House, the Colonial, Ocean Avenue Hotel, Ocean Front House, the Lawrence, the Ivy House, Bryn Mawr Hotel, Olive House, Buena Vista, Irvington House, the Ocean Wave, the Linwood, the Cordova, the Lillagaard, the Eldorado and the Sea Lovers Cottage. The Ocean Pier projects into the sea at Embury Avenue. Fire hydrants, water pipes and street widths (40 to 100 feet) are marked. East of Ocean Avenue the beach and the Atlantic Ocean fill the right third of the sheet, with the shore line drawn in blue. Scale 60 feet to an inch.","notes":["McClintock is McClintock Street and Olin is Olin Street today.","Ocean Avenue junctions are not used: only the street's west side is drawn and no width is printed.","Ocean Grove ocean front, McClintock to Broadway, Central Av to the beach. Pilot. 60 ft scale, one part. Ocean Av drawn with one side only (not used)."],"streetnames":["McClintock","Pitman Avenue","Olin","Main Avenue","Heck Avenue","Embury Avenue","Webb Avenue","Abbott Avenue","Broadway","Central Avenue","Beach Avenue","Ocean Avenue"],"placenames":["Ocean Grove","Atlantic Ocean"]},"sheet-52":{"description":"Sheet 52 covers the north-eastern corner of Ocean Grove, between Wesley Lake and McClintock Street and from Central Avenue to the ocean. Lake Avenue follows the south shore of Wesley Lake at the top left; below it Spray, Seaview, Atlantic, Surf and Bath avenues run from Central Avenue across Beach Avenue to Ocean Avenue. Ocean Pathway, a broad landscaped way with two park strips (blocks 11 and 12) between its two drives, leads from Central Avenue to the beach, and McClintock Street closes the sheet at the bottom. The blocks hold summer hotels and boarding houses: the Warrington, the Park View, the La Pierre, the Marlborough, the New Arborton, the Spray View Hotel, the Sea Side Hotel, the Sheldon (open during summer only, lit by electricity) with its annex, Surf Avenue House, the Brooklyn, the Aberdeen, the Gem, the Attic, the Norman, the Manchester, the Beach View, the Inskip House, the Waverly, the Ardmore, the Albatross, the Carrollton and the Lafayette. Ocean Avenue is drawn with its west side only, with the board walk and beach beyond and the Atlantic Ocean on the right. A block of Asbury Park (sheet 24) appears across the lake outlet at the top. Scale 60 feet to an inch.","notes":["McClintock is McClintock Street today.","Ocean Pathway is drawn wider than its two modern drives; its junctions were not used.","Ocean Grove north-east: Wesley Lake/Lake Av to McClintock, Central Av to the beach; Ocean Pathway left out (drawn wider than its two modern drives). 60 ft scale, one part."],"streetnames":["Lake Avenue","Spray Avenue","Seaview Avenue","Atlantic Avenue","Surf Avenue","Bath Avenue","Ocean Pathway","McClintock","Central Avenue","Beach Avenue","Ocean Avenue"],"placenames":["Ocean Grove","Wesley Lake","Atlantic Ocean"]},"sheet-53":{"description":"Sheet 53 covers the north-western part of the Ocean Grove camp meeting grounds along Wesley Lake, from Delaware Avenue to Central Avenue. The streets Delaware, New Jersey (lettered N. J. Av. where it bends along the lake), Pennsylvania and New York avenues and Pilgrim Pathway are crossed by Mount Tabor Way, Mount Carmel Way, Zion Way and Mount Pisgah Way, while Asbury Avenue and Lake Avenue run diagonally along the shore and Wesley Place, Thornley Place and Kingsley Place are short lanes near the lake. The centre of the sheet is the Ocean Grove Auditorium (seating capacity 10,000), with the Tabernacle, the Young People's Temple, the Model of Jerusalem, the Arlington, the Summer Pavilion and blocks of tents on the tenting grounds around it. Pilgrim Pathway passes in front of the Auditorium; Pitman Avenue, McClintock Street, the two drives of Ocean Pathway and Bath Avenue lead from it to Central Avenue at the bottom. An association yard with a tent house and storage house stands at Bath and Central avenues. Small cottages, the Howland House, Thornley Chapel, the Lakeside House and the Terrace Lodge fill the lakeside blocks. A foot bridge crosses Wesley Lake toward Asbury Park; the Asbury Park shore beyond it is only outlined and is left out of the mask. The sheet carries a bar for 100 feet to an inch, but its streets fit 60 feet to an inch like the other sheets.","notes":["Scale bar reads 100 ft to an inch, but the fitted scale (6.67 px/ft, 19 points) matches the 60 ft sheets: the bar is wrong.","Zion Way is Mount Zion Way today.","Wesley Place is a footway in OpenStreetMap.","Ocean Grove north-west along Wesley Lake: Auditorium, tenting grounds, Mt Tabor/Carmel/Zion/Pisgah Ways. Bar says 100 ft to an inch, but the fit (6.67 px/ft) matches the 60 ft sheets: bar wrong. One part."],"streetnames":["Delaware Avenue","New Jersey Avenue","Pennsylvania Avenue","New York Avenue","Pilgrim Pathway","Central Avenue","Mount Tabor Way","Mount Carmel Way","Zion Way","Mount Pisgah Way","Asbury Avenue","Lake Avenue","Wesley Place","Thornley Place","Kingsley Place","Pitman Avenue","McClintock","Ocean Pathway","Bath Avenue"],"placenames":["Ocean Grove","Wesley Lake"]}}}